It is not similar to `==`/`===`, if the left hand operand is signed then `>>>` performs sign extension.

```
reg signed [9:0] b = 10'sb11_0101_0101;
reg signed [9:0] a_signed;
reg        [9:0] a_unsigned;

always_comb begin
  a_signed   = b >>> 2;
  a_unsigned = b >>  2;
end
```

Result:

```
#a_signed   1111010101
#a_unsigned 0011010101
```

